/></a:bodyPr><a:lstStyle/><a:p><a:pPr><a:buClr><a:schemeClr val="bg1"/></a:buClr><a:buFont typeface="Wingdings" panose="05000000000000000000" pitchFamily="2" charset="2"/><a:buChar char="Ø"/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="2000" dirty="0"><a:solidFill><a:schemeClr val="bg1"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Franklin Gothic Book" panose="020B0503020102020204" pitchFamily="34" charset="0"/></a:rPr><a:t>How to provide care to an aging population</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:pPr lvl="1"><a:buClr><a:schemeClr val="bg1"/></a:buClr><a:buFont typeface="Wingdings" panose="05000000000000000000" pitchFamily="2" charset="2"/><a:buChar char="Ø"/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="1800" dirty="0"><a:solidFill><a:schemeClr val="bg1"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Franklin Gothic Book" panose="020B0503020102020204" pitchFamily="34" charset="0"/></a:rPr><a:t>Department of Public Health recommends 250 staffed acute care patient beds per 100,000.  CA average 224</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:pPr lvl="1"><a:buClr><a:schemeClr val="bg1"/></a:buClr><a:buFont typeface="Wingdings" panose="05000000000000000000" pitchFamily="2" charset="2"/><a:buChar char="Ø"/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="1800" dirty="0"><a:solidFill><a:schemeClr val="bg1"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Franklin Gothic Book" panose="020B0503020102020204" pitchFamily="34" charset="0"/></a:rPr><a:t>Treatment Advocacy Group recommends 50 psychiatric care beds per 100,000.  CA average 19</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:pPr><a:buClr><a:schemeClr val="bg1"/></a:buClr><a:buFont typeface="Wingdings" panose="05000000000000000000" pitchFamily="2" charset="2"/><a:buChar char="Ø"/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="2000" dirty="0"><a:solidFill><a:schemeClr val="bg1"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Franklin Gothic Book" panose="020B0503020102020204" pitchFamily="34" charset="0"/></a:rPr><a:t>Access to emergency care and primary care physicians</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:pPr lvl="1"><a:buClr><a:schemeClr val="bg1"/></a:buClr><a:buFont typeface="Wingdings" panose="05000000000000000000" pitchFamily="2" charset="2"/><a:buChar char="Ø"/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="1800" dirty="0"><a:solidFill><a:schemeClr val="bg1"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Franklin Gothic Book" panose="020B0503020102020204" pitchFamily="34" charset="0"/></a:rPr><a:t>CA ranks as one of the lowest nationally regarding number of emergency departments per capita (6.7 / 1M)  And one of the highest regarding emergency department wait times (5 hrs.) CA v. (1.5 hrs.) US</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:pPr lvl="1"><a:buClr><a:schemeClr val="bg1"/></a:buClr><a:buFont typeface="Wingdings" panose="05000000000000000000" pitchFamily="2" charset="2"/><a:buChar char="Ø"/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="1800" dirty="0"><a:solidFill><a:schemeClr val="bg1"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Franklin Gothic Book" panose="020B0503020102020204" pitchFamily="34" charset="0"/></a:rPr><a:t>Number of primary care physicians; (84 / 100,000) CA v. (86 / 100,000) US</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:pPr><a:buClr><a:schemeClr val="bg1"/></a:buClr><a:buFont typeface="Wingdings" panose="05000000000000000000" pitchFamily="2" charset="2"/><a:buChar char="Ø"/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="2000" dirty="0"><a:solidFill><a:schemeClr val="bg1"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Franklin Gothic Book" panose="020B0503020102020204" pitchFamily="34" charset="0"/></a:rPr><a:t>How to adapt to ever-changing demographics for each specific location</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:pPr lvl="1"><a:buClr><a:schemeClr val="bg1"/></a:buClr><a:buFont typeface="Wingdings" panose="05000000000000000000" pitchFamily="2" charset="2"/><a:buChar char="Ø"/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="1800" dirty="0"><a:solidFill><a:schemeClr val="bg1"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Franklin Gothic Book" panose="020B0503020102020204" pitchFamily="34" charset="0"/></a:rPr><a:t>Population density, growth, age, race, sex, and household income</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:pPr lvl="1"><a:buClr><a:schemeClr val="bg1"/></a:buClr><a:buFont typeface="Wingdings" panose="05000000000000000000" pitchFamily="2" charset="2"/><a:buChar char="Ø"/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="1800" dirty="0"><a:solidFill><a:schemeClr val="bg1"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Franklin Gothic Book" panose="020B0503020102020204" pitchFamily="34" charset="0"/></a:rPr><a:t>Health outcomes based on patient discharge data (Examples</a:t></a:r><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="1800" dirty="0"><a:solidFill><a:schemeClr val="bg1"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Franklin Gothic Book" panose="020B0503020102020204" pitchFamily="34" charset="0"/><a:sym typeface="Wingdings" panose="05000000000000000000" pitchFamily="2" charset="2"/></a:rPr><a:t>)</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:pPr lvl="2"><a:buClr><a:schemeClr val="bg1"/></a:buClr><a:buFont typeface="Wingdings" panose="05000000000000000000" pitchFamily="2" charset="2"/><a:buChar char="Ø"/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="1600" dirty="0"><a:solidFill><a:schemeClr val="bg1"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Franklin Gothic Book" panose="020B0503020102020204" pitchFamily="34" charset="0"/><a:sym typeface="Wingdings" panose="05000000000000000000" pitchFamily="2" charset="2"/></a:rPr><a:t>Cancer mortality, cervical cancer incidence, colon &amp; rectum cancer incidence, diabetes prevalence, heart disease mortality, lung disease mortality, motor vehicle crash death, obesity (adult), overweight (adult), pedestrian motor vehicle death, poor dental health, poor general health, disabilities, premature death, stroke mortality, suicide…</a:t></a:r></a:p></p:txBody></p:sp><p:pic><p:nvPicPr><p:cNvPr id="6" name="Picture 5"><a:extLst><a:ext uri="{FF2B5EF4-FFF2-40B4-BE49-F238E27FC236}"><a16:creationId xmlns:a16="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/drawing/2014/main" id="{35003987-0719-02DB-A45F-8A4932407FE5}"/></a:ext></a:extLst></p:cNvPr><p:cNvPicPr><a:picLocks noChangeAspect="1"/></p:cNvPicPr><p:nvPr/></p:nvPicPr><p:blipFill><a:blip r:embed="rId2"><a:extLst><a:ext u